1
00:00:00,375 --> 00:00:02,001
[Bernadette] Previously on
The Big Bang Theory...

2
00:00:02,961 --> 00:00:06,214
I was offered a summer research fellowship
at Princeton.

3
00:00:08,341 --> 00:00:11,886
Princeton, a fine institution.

4
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:15,390
The place where Albert Einstein taught

5
00:00:15,557 --> 00:00:19,310
and where Leonard got his PhD,
so it may have gone downhill.

6
00:00:21,938 --> 00:00:26,234
Just remember, I'm proud of you
and I support you in all that you do.

7
00:00:26,943 --> 00:00:28,361
Thank you, that means a lot.

8
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:32,365
Oh, and one last thing, if you find
yourself working with a male scientist

9
00:00:32,532 --> 00:00:36,745
who's as smart as me, as tall as me,
and has hair like Thor,

10
00:00:36,911 --> 00:00:40,498
well, then, I want you to step away from
the situation and call me immediately.

11
00:00:44,127 --> 00:00:45,462
How are you settling in?

12
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:48,590
Pretty well.
Princeton has a beautiful campus.

13
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:50,842
You know, I've learned some fun facts
about New Jersey,

14
00:00:51,009 --> 00:00:52,010
to help you make small talk.

15
00:00:52,927 --> 00:00:56,139
Would you like to know the state bird
or the murder rate?

16
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:59,059
They're both shocking.

17
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:02,687
Actually, I want to hear about you.

18
00:01:02,854 --> 00:01:04,022
How are things at home?

19
00:01:04,189 --> 00:01:07,734
Well, I'm a lot less likely to see
an Eastern Goldfinch or be murdered,

20
00:01:07,901 --> 00:01:08,943
I'll tell you that.

21
00:01:10,653 --> 00:01:11,738
I miss you.

22
00:01:11,905 --> 00:01:13,114
I miss you, too.

23
00:01:13,281 --> 00:01:16,868
It's so strange, earlier today,
I ended a sentence with a preposition,

24
00:01:17,035 --> 00:01:19,662
and you weren't there
to correct my grammar.

25
00:01:19,829 --> 00:01:22,248
I am sorry you had to go through that.

26
00:01:24,125 --> 00:01:27,796
In fact,
that's when I started to really miss you.

27
00:01:29,672 --> 00:01:32,133
You know you just split an infinitive.

28
00:01:33,301 --> 00:01:37,096
Did I? Are you going to teach me a lesson?

29
00:01:39,974 --> 00:01:41,142
I am!

30
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:46,648
It is naughty to put an adverb
between the word "to" and the verb stem.

31
00:01:48,149 --> 00:01:50,068
What are you going to do about it?

32
00:01:50,985 --> 00:01:52,987
I'm going to admonish you.

33
00:01:54,322 --> 00:01:55,824
Vigorously?

34
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,536
That's the only kind of admonishing I do.

35
00:02:00,995 --> 00:02:02,997
[theme song playing]

36
00:02:25,395 --> 00:02:27,105
How's Sheldon doing with Amy gone?

37
00:02:27,272 --> 00:02:30,275
Well, the last three nights,
I've had to take him to get a haircut,

38
00:02:30,441 --> 00:02:33,027
to the train store
and to a Walgreens in Arcadia,

39
00:02:33,194 --> 00:02:35,738
where they still have
the "good ibuprofen."

40
00:02:36,948 --> 00:02:39,367
Now ask me how I'm doing with Amy gone.

41
00:02:39,534 --> 00:02:40,952
-How are you doing with--
-Shut up.

42
00:02:42,996 --> 00:02:45,331
If you'd like, we can help you out.
[chuckles softly]

43
00:02:45,498 --> 00:02:46,499
Oh, that would be great.

44
00:02:46,666 --> 00:02:48,001
I mean, not me, I've got a wife and child,

45
00:02:48,167 --> 00:02:51,462
but this one posts video of himself
flossing on Instagram.

46
00:02:53,256 --> 00:02:55,008
It was a tutorial.

47
00:02:56,593 --> 00:02:58,678
And, yes, I'm happy to keep
Sheldon company.

48
00:02:58,845 --> 00:03:01,472
Great, tonight he wants to look at ladders
at Home Depot.

49
00:03:01,639 --> 00:03:02,640
Oh, why does he need a ladder?

50
00:03:02,807 --> 00:03:06,019
He doesn't, he just likes looking at them,
bring a book.

51
00:03:06,853 --> 00:03:11,524
Gentlemen, you may remember Dr. Nowitzki,
she's back at Caltech for her postdoc.

52
00:03:11,691 --> 00:03:12,901
[Leonard] Hello.

53
00:03:12,984 --> 00:03:14,360
[Raj] Hi.
Oh, let me bring a chair for you.

54
00:03:14,527 --> 00:03:18,323
Oh, thanks. Dr. Nowitzki is going to
tell me about the work she did at CERN.

55
00:03:18,489 --> 00:03:21,951
And she brought me
this duty-free Toblerone.

56
00:03:22,535 --> 00:03:23,745
[chuckles] Oh, I love those!

57
00:03:24,579 --> 00:03:25,914
Let's sit somewhere else.

58
00:03:30,627 --> 00:03:32,211
What just happened?

59
00:03:33,755 --> 00:03:36,299
A stranger just lured Sheldon away
with a candy bar.

60
00:03:38,801 --> 00:03:41,137
Isn't she the grad student
that used to follow him around?

61
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:45,725
Oh, yeah, back before he hit puberty
and grew man parts.

62
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:46,851
[Leonard chuckles]

63
00:03:47,268 --> 00:03:49,187
So, what do you guys think that's about?

64
00:03:49,354 --> 00:03:50,897
Knowing Sheldon, nothing.

65
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:54,067
So, tell me about
your scalar dark energy experiment.

66
00:03:54,233 --> 00:03:57,028
Not till you tell me about
your latest paper on quantum loop theory.

67
00:03:57,445 --> 00:04:00,365
Oh. You must be one of those
dessert-before-dinner people.

68
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:01,491
[chuckles]

69
00:04:03,451 --> 00:04:05,620
He just made her laugh, something's wrong.

70
00:04:06,913 --> 00:04:09,249
Do you see the way she's looking at him?

71
00:04:09,582 --> 00:04:12,377
Yeah. Like Bernadette used to look at me.

72
00:04:12,543 --> 00:04:15,255
I keep telling you,
close the bathroom door.

73
00:04:17,632 --> 00:04:18,925
Oh, did you see that?

74
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:21,427
She just touched his hand
and he didn't swat it away.

75
00:04:21,594 --> 00:04:23,096
What is happening?

76
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:27,058
Okay, the simplest explanation
is usually the right one.

77
00:04:28,226 --> 00:04:30,436
-Which is?
-That ain't Sheldon.

78
00:04:34,774 --> 00:04:37,986
Not only did they eat together,
Leonard said he made her laugh!

79
00:04:38,152 --> 00:04:41,114
That's nothing,
Howie said she touched his hand.

80
00:04:41,281 --> 00:04:42,448
What? Did he Purell?

81
00:04:43,449 --> 00:04:44,450
No.

82
00:04:46,286 --> 00:04:48,288
I cannot believe Leonard
mentioned the Toblerone,

83
00:04:48,454 --> 00:04:50,123
but left that part out.

84
00:04:51,124 --> 00:04:52,208
Should we call Amy?

85
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:54,836
I don't know,
we shouldn't worry her if it's nothing.

86
00:04:55,003 --> 00:04:57,130
I guess we could wait
till we have more information

87
00:04:57,296 --> 00:04:59,465
-about this girl.
-Yeah. [sighs]

88
00:04:59,924 --> 00:05:05,013
Do you think living with Amy has somehow
stirred up Sheldon's sexual appetite?

89
00:05:06,597 --> 00:05:07,598
Ugh!

90
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:14,022
How can you think that?

91
00:05:16,107 --> 00:05:18,735
Why would you even
put those words together?

92
00:05:18,901 --> 00:05:21,320
All right, then we agree,
he's not making any moves,

93
00:05:21,487 --> 00:05:23,197
it's this Dr. Ramona chick.

94
00:05:23,656 --> 00:05:26,409
Nowitzki. I googled her,
she's pretty cute.

95
00:05:26,743 --> 00:05:30,580
Really? All I got from Leonard was,
"The Toblerone bar had nuts."

96
00:05:33,791 --> 00:05:38,504
Oh! And get this, I saw an articulating
ladder with dual-leg leveling,

97
00:05:38,671 --> 00:05:42,091
which delivers stability
and adaptability to uneven terrain.

98
00:05:43,342 --> 00:05:45,261
Sounds like a big night.

99
00:05:45,845 --> 00:05:48,014
Raj made the funniest joke, he said,

100
00:05:48,181 --> 00:05:51,601
"Which is the best ladder to use
to hang myself?" [laughs]

101
00:05:54,854 --> 00:05:57,231
So you're keeping busy, you're not lonely?

102
00:05:57,732 --> 00:06:01,152
Not at all. No, I've had outings with
Leonard and Raj in the evening,

103
00:06:01,319 --> 00:06:03,738
and, oh, I had lunch with Dr. Nowitzki.

104
00:06:03,905 --> 00:06:04,906
Who's he?

105
00:06:05,073 --> 00:06:06,616
Oh, no, Dr. Nowitzki is a woman.

106
00:06:07,366 --> 00:06:09,077
Oh, really? When did you meet her?

107
00:06:09,327 --> 00:06:11,746
Many years ago,
back when she was a grad student.

108
00:06:11,913 --> 00:06:15,917
She's always been a huge fan of my work,
and now she's doing research at Caltech.

109
00:06:17,585 --> 00:06:19,212
"Huge fan" you say?

110
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:22,173
Yes. I think you'd like her.

111
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:25,051
She's extremely intelligent,
just like you.

112
00:06:25,551 --> 00:06:29,388
Unlike you, she's tall, blonde
and used to be an Olympic swimmer.

113
00:06:32,975 --> 00:06:34,560
That's terrific, I'll call you right back.

114
00:06:35,937 --> 00:06:37,563
[ringtone playing on laptop]

115
00:06:37,897 --> 00:06:40,942
-Oh, hey, Amy.
-I gave you one job!

116
00:06:43,152 --> 00:06:45,863
Keep an eye on him! How hard is that?

117
00:06:46,948 --> 00:06:50,118
We thought you meant
not letting him run out into traffic.

118
00:06:52,245 --> 00:06:54,163
Which he only did once.

119
00:06:55,998 --> 00:06:57,291
Why didn't you tell me?

120
00:06:57,458 --> 00:06:59,043
We didn't want you to worry.

121
00:06:59,210 --> 00:07:00,711
Should I worry?

122
00:07:00,878 --> 00:07:03,798
No, come on, it's Sheldon,
nothing is going to happen.

123
00:07:03,965 --> 00:07:05,883
That's what you said to me
when I started dating him.

124
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:09,387
And then five years later,
bingo-bango, something happened!

125
00:07:10,304 --> 00:07:12,265
Yeah, but you're going to be back
in three months.

126
00:07:12,431 --> 00:07:13,766
[sighs] You don't get it.

127
00:07:13,933 --> 00:07:16,436
I've been smacking that ketchup bottle
for a long time.

128
00:07:16,602 --> 00:07:20,106
All she's got to do is tip it over
and point it at her fries!

129
00:07:21,607 --> 00:07:22,775
What do you want us to do?

130
00:07:22,942 --> 00:07:24,360
I don't know!

131
00:07:24,652 --> 00:07:26,529
Might be the New Jersey talking,

132
00:07:26,696 --> 00:07:29,490
but this Nowitzki broad
needs to disappear.

133
00:07:30,992 --> 00:07:32,160
That's ridiculous.

134
00:07:32,326 --> 00:07:35,997
As far as we know, all that happened is
two scientists had lunch.

135
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:39,792
Yeah, but one of those scientists is
a tall, blonde Olympic swimmer!

136
00:07:39,959 --> 00:07:42,462
Oh, come on,
looks don't matter to Sheldon.

137
00:07:43,796 --> 00:07:46,174
Because he only has eyes for you.

138
00:07:48,634 --> 00:07:50,845
-Nice try.
-Thanks, I was scrambling.

139
00:07:54,807 --> 00:07:55,975
It's unbelievable.

140
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:59,896
Sheldon has lunch with another woman,
and somehow my wife yells at me.

141
00:08:00,813 --> 00:08:02,148
Penny laid into me, too.

142
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:06,235
Apparently, I'm overly fixated
on premium Swiss chocolate bars.

143
00:08:08,029 --> 00:08:09,655
Can you even eat those things?

144
00:08:09,822 --> 00:08:13,201
Mmm, if I take a LACTAID a half-hour
before and some Pepto right after.

145
00:08:13,659 --> 00:08:15,119
Sounds like a lot of work.

146
00:08:15,786 --> 00:08:17,038
Huh, I'm worth it.

147
00:08:17,121 --> 00:08:18,122
[chuckles]

148
00:08:18,706 --> 00:08:21,709
Guys, focus.
Should we do something about Nowitzki?

149
00:08:21,876 --> 00:08:23,753
-Like what?
-[Raj sighs]

150
00:08:24,086 --> 00:08:27,465
Uh, well, she's single,
so if somebody else asks her out,

151
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:30,343
and she says yes,
then we know she's not into Sheldon.

152
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:31,761
I'll do it.

153
00:08:37,725 --> 00:08:40,603
No offense, Stuart,
but the woman's a doctor.

154
00:08:41,479 --> 00:08:43,231
So? Doctors like me.

155
00:08:43,981 --> 00:08:48,027
Whenever I see mine, he calls in
a bunch of other doctors to have a look.

156
00:08:51,113 --> 00:08:53,199
She's not that kind of doctor.

157
00:08:53,950 --> 00:08:55,117
Oh. Well, her loss.

158
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:58,287
I have been called
"a genuine medical oddity."

159
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:06,420
-Actually, I was going to suggest me.
-[scoffs]

160
00:09:06,587 --> 00:09:09,048
Great, anybody's better than... [mumbles]

161
00:09:11,384 --> 00:09:15,388
Excuse me, they took out my spleen
and gallbladder, not my feelings.

162
00:09:21,227 --> 00:09:22,728
[exhales and clears throat]

163
00:09:24,063 --> 00:09:27,024
-Dr. Nowitzki, good to see you.
-Good to see you, too.

164
00:09:27,191 --> 00:09:28,401
May I join you?

165
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:29,860
No.

166
00:09:33,447 --> 00:09:34,574
Good to see you.

167
00:09:37,743 --> 00:09:40,121
We should call Guinness,
that might be a record.

168
00:09:41,372 --> 00:09:45,376
She's clearly having a working lunch
and preferred to eat alone.

169
00:09:46,335 --> 00:09:48,337
Dr. Cooper, over here!

170
00:09:50,256 --> 00:09:52,592
I could have made her very happy.

171
00:09:54,093 --> 00:09:56,178
You kept walking, I think you did.

172
00:09:59,557 --> 00:10:01,142
You really think
there's reason to worry?

173
00:10:01,309 --> 00:10:03,477
Yeah, she's definitely
going after Sheldon.

174
00:10:03,644 --> 00:10:05,479
[sighs] I made a play for her,
and she shot me down.

175
00:10:05,646 --> 00:10:07,607
All right, well,
that doesn't prove anything.

176
00:10:07,773 --> 00:10:11,277
Yeah, there's a million reasons
a woman would shoot Raj down.

177
00:10:13,404 --> 00:10:14,780
Like, really, a million?

178
00:10:14,947 --> 00:10:15,948
Fine, hundreds.

179
00:10:16,115 --> 00:10:17,450
Thank you.

180
00:10:18,451 --> 00:10:21,954
The point is, this could be nothing
and we are all overreacting.

181
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:25,958
Hey, everybody, this is my friend,
Dr. Nowitzki.

182
00:10:26,125 --> 00:10:27,293
Hi.

183
00:10:27,460 --> 00:10:28,544
[all] Hi.

184
00:10:30,504 --> 00:10:32,632
We just went swimming.

185
00:10:35,968 --> 00:10:37,511
You actually got in a pool?

186
00:10:38,179 --> 00:10:39,263
I was scared,

187
00:10:39,430 --> 00:10:42,892
but I told myself,
"It's just a big bathtub."

188
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:45,936
Then I got scared again
'cause there are all these strangers

189
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:47,021
-in my bathtub.
-[chuckles]

190
00:10:48,314 --> 00:10:49,357
I was proud of him.

191
00:10:49,523 --> 00:10:52,193
A lot of people don't put
their face in the water on the first day.

192
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:54,862
I was hiding from a bee,
but it still counts.

193
00:10:57,365 --> 00:10:59,325
Can I just squeeze in here?

194
00:11:03,329 --> 00:11:05,247
So, Sheldon, have you talked to Amy?

195
00:11:05,414 --> 00:11:06,540
Yes, we skyped this morning,

196
00:11:06,707 --> 00:11:08,459
and I'm sure I'll check in with her
before I go to sleep.

197
00:11:08,626 --> 00:11:10,378
Sheldon talks about her all the time.

198
00:11:10,544 --> 00:11:11,712
I can't wait to meet her.

199
00:11:11,879 --> 00:11:12,880
No... That is true,

200
00:11:13,047 --> 00:11:15,883
she keeps asking
how long Amy's going to be gone.

201
00:11:18,344 --> 00:11:21,972
Uh, so, Ramona, tell us about yourself,
do you have a boyfriend?

202
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:26,060
Leonard! Your wife is sitting right here,
what are you doing?

203
00:11:28,896 --> 00:11:31,357
No, my work doesn't leave me a lot of time
for relationships.

204
00:11:31,524 --> 00:11:33,692
I think you made that very clear.

205
00:11:35,069 --> 00:11:37,488
She was part of the American team at CERN.

206
00:11:37,655 --> 00:11:40,241
I had a front-row seat
when they detected the Higgs boson.

207
00:11:41,033 --> 00:11:43,786
Do you know,
I've corresponded with Peter Higgs.

208
00:11:43,953 --> 00:11:45,246
Would you like to see some of his letters?

209
00:11:45,413 --> 00:11:47,248
-Absolutely.
-I'll get them.

210
00:11:47,581 --> 00:11:49,750
Well, hang on, I'll come with you.

211
00:11:50,167 --> 00:11:52,086
Oh, fun, like a playdate.

212
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:55,172
[door closes]

213
00:11:55,423 --> 00:11:56,424
Okay, correct me if I'm wrong,

214
00:11:56,590 --> 00:11:59,635
but isn't that exactly what we were
supposed to stop from happening?

215
00:12:01,053 --> 00:12:02,096
I threw my body at them!

216
00:12:02,263 --> 00:12:04,265
What else did you want me to do?

217
00:12:05,015 --> 00:12:06,016
[Penny sighs]

218
00:12:06,267 --> 00:12:07,601
You think you should call Amy?

219
00:12:07,768 --> 00:12:09,770
You got fingers and a mouth, you call her.

220
00:12:13,482 --> 00:12:14,900
Here you go.

221
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:17,111
Are these all from Peter Higgs?

222
00:12:17,278 --> 00:12:19,196
Oh, no, no.
They're from many famous people.

223
00:12:19,613 --> 00:12:21,991
See? Oh, like this one.
This is from Patrick Stewart.

224
00:12:22,158 --> 00:12:26,745
It says if I come to his house again,
I get to meet his dogs.

225
00:12:27,079 --> 00:12:28,080
[chuckles]

226
00:12:28,664 --> 00:12:30,499
[ringtone playing on laptop]

227
00:12:30,875 --> 00:12:32,209
Oh, excuse me.

228
00:12:35,254 --> 00:12:37,089
-Hello, Sheldon.
-Oh, hello, Amy.

229
00:12:37,923 --> 00:12:39,592
I was missing you again.

230
00:12:39,758 --> 00:12:42,720
I miss you, too. Hey! This is good timing.

231
00:12:42,887 --> 00:12:45,431
You remember that Dr. Nowitzki
I told you about?

232
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:46,932
She's right here!

233
00:12:48,392 --> 00:12:49,768
[stutters] She's what?

234
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:53,481
Hello.

235
00:12:54,106 --> 00:12:55,149
Hi.

236
00:12:55,566 --> 00:12:56,984
So nice to meet you.

237
00:12:57,735 --> 00:12:58,736
Uh-huh.

238
00:13:00,321 --> 00:13:01,739
[cell phone ringing]

239
00:13:01,989 --> 00:13:04,492
Hang on. Hello?

240
00:13:05,993 --> 00:13:07,786
Little late, Leonard!

241
00:13:09,288 --> 00:13:10,331
Sorry.

242
00:13:10,498 --> 00:13:12,666
What is Leonard doing
calling you at this hour?

243
00:13:13,375 --> 00:13:14,835
It's not important.

244
00:13:15,252 --> 00:13:18,714
I must tell you,
that seems a little inappropriate.

245
00:13:18,881 --> 00:13:20,799
-Don't you agree?
-I do.

246
00:13:20,966 --> 00:13:22,343
See?

247
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:24,345
We both think so.

248
00:13:27,014 --> 00:13:29,683
All right, this is making me crazy.
Somebody's got to go over there.

249
00:13:30,184 --> 00:13:32,353
You've got feet and legs, you do it.

250
00:13:35,189 --> 00:13:36,190
Will you go with me?

251
00:13:36,357 --> 00:13:39,193
To do what,
shake a can of nickels at them?

252
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:42,613
We're being ridiculous.

253
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:47,159
There's no way a woman that attractive
is trying to seduce Sheldon Cooper.

254
00:13:48,827 --> 00:13:51,539
You done
trying to make yourself feel better?

255
00:13:52,206 --> 00:13:54,708
No, I haven't played the race card yet.

256
00:13:57,336 --> 00:13:59,505
Hey. I hate to break up the party,

257
00:13:59,672 --> 00:14:02,967
but Amy says I'm tired
and have to go to bed.

258
00:14:05,135 --> 00:14:07,304
It was nice seeing everybody.
Thank you for dinner.

259
00:14:07,471 --> 00:14:08,556
-Sure.
-Pleasure.

260
00:14:08,722 --> 00:14:09,932
Whatever.

261
00:14:11,976 --> 00:14:13,852
-Walk me to my car?
-Of course.

262
00:14:14,186 --> 00:14:15,646
We'll all go!

263
00:14:32,037 --> 00:14:33,205
Excuse me.

264
00:14:44,925 --> 00:14:46,802
Pardon, I just need to... Yeah.

265
00:14:57,563 --> 00:15:00,065
[chuckles] That was fun, like Mario Kart.

266
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:05,988
Bye.

267
00:15:07,072 --> 00:15:08,198
We need to talk.

268
00:15:08,824 --> 00:15:11,619
Is this about Leonard and Amy?
I don't like it either.

269
00:15:15,581 --> 00:15:18,083
Okay, I know you don't have
a lot of experience with women,

270
00:15:18,250 --> 00:15:21,211
but Ramona
seems to have a romantic interest in you.

271
00:15:21,962 --> 00:15:24,715
That doesn't make any sense,
she knows I have a girlfriend.

272
00:15:24,882 --> 00:15:26,925
Well, sometimes women don't care.

273
00:15:27,092 --> 00:15:28,928
Sometimes it makes them want a guy
even more.

274
00:15:30,596 --> 00:15:33,682
Look, that may be true,
but Dr. Nowitzki's just a friend.

275
00:15:33,849 --> 00:15:36,185
In fact, I wouldn't have even noticed
she's a woman

276
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:39,480
if she hadn't worn that bathing suit
that highlighted her bosom.

277
00:15:43,067 --> 00:15:45,069
Okay, um, [clears throat]
let's try this,

278
00:15:45,235 --> 00:15:48,113
think of yourself as one of those
limited edition toys

279
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:49,365
people like to collect.

280
00:15:50,574 --> 00:15:51,909
I already do.

281
00:15:54,203 --> 00:15:55,496
Well, then you get it.

282
00:15:56,121 --> 00:15:59,458
Oh! Because there's only one of me,
I'm more valuable.

283
00:15:59,625 --> 00:16:00,793
Right.

284
00:16:01,085 --> 00:16:02,127
Although,

285
00:16:02,294 --> 00:16:06,006
Amy's already taken me out of my package
and played with me.

286
00:16:09,968 --> 00:16:12,388
Let's forget the toy thing, okay?
Uh, maybe--

287
00:16:12,554 --> 00:16:16,934
Penny, look, I appreciate your concern,
but I don't think that's what's happening.

288
00:16:17,476 --> 00:16:19,812
All right, what do you think is happening?

289
00:16:20,396 --> 00:16:22,898
I think Dr. Nowitzki
is a friendly colleague.

290
00:16:23,649 --> 00:16:26,652
I think you and Leonard
need to see a marriage counselor.

291
00:16:28,195 --> 00:16:32,032
And I need to update my resume
to include swimming as a special skill.

292
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:36,662
[door closes]

293
00:16:40,165 --> 00:16:42,626
Don't look at me like that, I tried!

294
00:16:45,713 --> 00:16:46,714
[knock on door]

295
00:16:47,798 --> 00:16:49,007
Hey, did you eat yet?

296
00:16:49,633 --> 00:16:51,385
Ah, breakfast, yes, lunch, no.

297
00:16:51,552 --> 00:16:52,761
I did have a cough drop,

298
00:16:52,928 --> 00:16:56,140
but that really rides the line
between sucking and eating.

299
00:16:57,307 --> 00:16:58,934
Well, perfect. I made us sandwiches.

300
00:16:59,101 --> 00:17:00,644
How thoughtful.

301
00:17:00,811 --> 00:17:02,855
-Thank you.
-No big deal,

302
00:17:03,021 --> 00:17:04,690
I enjoy spending time with you.

303
00:17:04,857 --> 00:17:06,567
And I with you.

304
00:17:08,193 --> 00:17:09,528
Question.

305
00:17:09,653 --> 00:17:12,448
Are you seeking
a romantic relationship with me?

306
00:17:14,032 --> 00:17:15,159
What if I were?

307
00:17:16,201 --> 00:17:18,454
Well, that would raise
a number of problems.

308
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:21,123
We're colleagues, I'm currently in a--

309
00:17:30,299 --> 00:17:31,675
Excuse me a moment.

310
00:18:06,001 --> 00:18:07,669
[chuckles]

311
00:18:31,652 --> 00:18:34,863
-[knocking]
-Amy? Amy. Amy.

312
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:53,423
Will you marry me?

